{"calculus_ref":"stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md","clause_relations":[{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Objects, relations, constraints, latitude, residuals, traversals, transformations, projections and judgments retain their declared semantic, operation, evaluation and decision authority. Copying, interpreting, encoding, evaluating or transporting a record does not transfer authority.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P4b","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-005-copying-transfers-no-authority"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:latitude-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:transformation-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Two values may differ lawfully only through an applicable latitude record or transformation relation. An implementation preference, a probabilistic choice or a human presence is not implicit latitude.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P1","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:latitude-must-be-declared","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-008-difference-only-through-latitude-or-transformation"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:residual-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Every material uncertainty, omission, translation loss, unresolved boundary or unproven relation remains in the residual set until an authorised disposition creates an exact successor model. Absence from a projection is not resolution.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-009-absence-from-projection-is-not-resolution"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:transformation-application","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:transformation-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Application is T[t](M_b, inputs) -> M_b_prime* | hold | gap | refusal. The exact transformation identity t declares every mutation it may perform. The input model remains unchanged; M_b_prime* is a proposed successor, and a proposed successor does not accept or admit itself. FOUNDATIONS section 4 consumes this law as the conservation accounting of every step.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:transformation-records-accounting","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-application-proposes-and-never-self-admits"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:local-record-delta","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:transformation-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"With Local_b the complete input local-record identity set, P_t preserved, R_t removed and N_t introduced: Local_b = P_t disjoint_union R_t; Local_b_prime = P_t disjoint_union N_t; N_t intersect Local_b = empty; R_t intersect Local_b_prime = empty. Every removed identity is absent from the successor; every introduced identity is absent from the input and carries a complete lawful record in exactly one successor population; every input local-record identity is classified exactly once as preserved or removed; no local record is silently dropped, retained or duplicated.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-closed-local-record-delta"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:transformation-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:operation-authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"t.traversal resolves one v; the context, owner, scope, basis, operation authority, evidence, provenance and stop contract of t equal or lawfully restrict the corresponding traversal coordinates. A broader or mismatched coordinate refuses.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-coordinates-equal-or-restrict-the-traversal"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:external-resolution-witness","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:transformation-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The external-resolution coordinates form a distinct closed delta: E_b = EP_t disjoint_union ER_t; E_b_prime = EP_t disjoint_union EN_t; EN_t intersect E_b = empty; ER_t intersect E_b_prime = empty. For every preserved resolution x, external_resolution_witnesses contains exactly one witness {external_resolution, domain_model, codomain_model, domain_resolution, codomain_resolution, decision: equal, evidence} whose two tuples are exactly field-equal. A nominally equal identifier, equivalent or changed target, changed target kind, reference domain, basis relation or resolution basis, or a missing witness cannot enter EP_t; a changed external resolution is a removal followed by introduction of the new resolution coordinate. Witnesses are total and unique over EP_t.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b, P3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-external-resolution-delta-and-witnesses"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:transformation-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"domain_model and codomain_model resolve exact content identities of the complete input and proposed successor models. Each model identity commits to its exact calculus basis, signature identity, complete finite population, complete external reference set, exact external-resolution map and selected model-content identity. A mutable locator, a model-family name, a partial projection or a population digest without the exact model identity refuses.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-model-identities-are-exact"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:preservation-relation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:transformation-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"preservation_relation resolves one exact typed equality relation applicable to the declared domain and codomain model identities and record kinds; it binds both model identities, both exact bases, the comparison domain, direction, authority, scope, evidence and equality law. Equivalence or meaning-preservation may relate a removed identity to an introduced identity; it cannot retain one identity in preserved.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P1, P3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-preservation-relation-is-exact-typed-equality"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:local-record-delta","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:preservation-relation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"For every preserved identity the input and successor records have the same record kind, identity, context, owner, scope and basis, and are either byte-identical under one exact canonical record grammar selected for both models, or equal under the exact preservation_relation when the records share no such byte grammar. A changed field, changed basis, changed record kind, nominally equal identifier, equivalence or unbound assertion of preserved meaning refuses membership in preserved.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P3, P1","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-preserved-identity-is-proven-equal"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:transformation-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:residual","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Material residuals remain in the successor residual set unless an exact authorised disposition is included in the transformation evidence. Failure to establish any model identity, basis, population, local or external partition, equality, external-resolution witness, residual or codomain equation refuses.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b, P5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-residuals-survive-unless-disposed"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:transformation-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:basis","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"For an ordinary same-basis transformation the domain model, the codomain model, t and its traversal share one basis and the two models share one signature. A cross-basis or cross-signature migration requires a separately identified transformation specialisation whose exact composite-basis and compatible signature-extension relations name both sides. No identity whose basis or record kind changes belongs to preserved: the source identity is removed and the successor identity introduced, their continuity represented only by the exact migration relation.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P3, P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-same-basis-or-separately-identified-migration"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:transformation-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A transformation is an operation-bearing specialisation of one exact traversal record v. Its record carries exactly: id, traversal, domain_model, codomain_model, context, owner, scope, basis, operation_authority, preconditions, preservation_relation, preserved, introduced, removed, external_preserved, external_introduced, external_removed, external_resolution_witnesses, residuals, evidence, provenance, stop_states, invalidation, re_entry.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b, P3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-transformation-record-fields"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:judgment-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:promotion-relation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Issuing a judgment does not transform, rewrite, reissue or rename its subject. Promotion is an explicit relation between the unchanged subject and its admission or acceptance judgment.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-014-judgment-never-transforms-its-subject"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:judgment-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:judgment","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A judgment points to an unchanged subject; it is the Judgment of FOUNDATIONS section 2 carried as a model record with exactly: id, kind, subject, subject_digest, context, owner, scope, basis, evaluator, authority, decision, evidence, provenance, decided_at.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-014-judgment-record-fields"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:latitude","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Two values differ lawfully only through a declared latitude or transformation relation; preference, probabilistic choice and human presence are not implicit latitude.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:latitude-must-be-declared"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:latitude-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:latitude","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Latitude = {id, applies_to, allowed_variation, forbidden_variation, context, owner, scope, basis, invalidation}. Silence is not latitude. Latitude grants no authority beyond its owner, scope, basis and invalidation law.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:latitude-record-is-explicit-and-bounded"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:residual-record","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:residual","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Residual = {id, subject, kind, uncertainty, consequence, context, owner, scope, basis, re_entry, invalidation}. Projection, compression, interpretation or encoding cannot erase a residual: it remains represented, is explicitly dispositioned by competent authority, or causes refusal. An undeclared residual kind or value refuses structural admission.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b, P6, P3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:residual-record-cannot-be-erased"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:conservation-accounting","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Every transformation records what it preserved, introduced and removed, its external resolution witnesses and its residuals.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:transformation-records-accounting"}],"closure":{"clauses":["urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-005-copying-transfers-no-authority","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-008-difference-only-through-latitude-or-transformation","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-009-absence-from-projection-is-not-resolution","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-application-proposes-and-never-self-admits","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-closed-local-record-delta","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-coordinates-equal-or-restrict-the-traversal","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-external-resolution-delta-and-witnesses","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-model-identities-are-exact","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-preservation-relation-is-exact-typed-equality","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-preserved-identity-is-proven-equal","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-residuals-survive-unless-disposed","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-same-basis-or-separately-identified-migration","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-013-transformation-record-fields","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-014-judgment-never-transforms-its-subject","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:ac-014-judgment-record-fields","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c